{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/960537-which-gamelines-splats-do-you-want-to-incorporate-sorcerers-more-often","id":960537,"title":"Which Gamelines/splats do you want to Incorporate Sorcerers more often?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-30T10:39:44-07:00","id":960537,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Which Gamelines/splats do you want to Incorporate Sorcerers more often?","content":"I really hope 4th ed incorporates Sorcerers as a general World of Darkness option found all over the place, rather then just with mages. I would like if they kept that the backbone of Traditions and Technocrats were Sorcerers, it does make Mages seem rarer and cooler if there were less of them then weaker magic users. So there would be three times more sorcerers then awakened, and 10 times more normal acolytes.<br /> <br /> I would have Werewolf maintain some kinfolk as maintainers of the knowledge so moderate sized septs maintain at least one shaman with at least one apprentice among the kinfolk along with it being common for Theurges to also learn sorcery. And certain camps and tribes, like the Uktena and Bubasti have common to pick up sorcery. Glasswalkers would have sorcery and enlightened science, and an even greater concentration in Camps like the Cyberdogs.<br /> <br /> I would have Tremere have a large Sorcerer population among their ghouls, as they retained all their troves of scrolls and grimoires from when they were a Mage house, this would exponentially improve their standing as the Blood Sorcerer Monopoly guys, now ghouls can actually contribute to the maintaining chantries beyond just fetching supplies. They could even bolster their alchemical and magical supplies by having mortals refine rare reagents for them.<br /> <br /> I would have Setites have both Sorcerers and Mages among their cults, as they exist not just as a Vampire clan but a religion.<br /> <br /> And Laibon had the setting just rife with Sorcerers, so much so they didn't feel like incorporating the sorcery rules and just used dumbed down rituals. I would toss that and use the flat out sorcerery rules to represent sorcerers.<br /> <br /> And i would have Ghoul organizations and mystically inclined Revenant families hoard sorcery, probably also use Alchemy to in fertility rituals. The Giovanni and Rosalinni families should have retained a lot of Sorcery in their mortal families, and the Rosilinni knew more then just necromancy.<br /> <br /> Pentex I would have filled with both Sorcery and Enlightened Science as they were probably the biggest organization that combined the two.<br /> <br /> Thoughts and suggestions?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T13:15:56-07:00","id":960631,"title":"","content":"To me one of the great things about Sorcerors is that you can slot them in just about anywhere. They're excellent all purpose genre crossing NPCs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T15:21:10-07:00","id":960705,"title":"","content":"Yes, you just have to add Virtues and Humanity when you add them to VtM.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T14:23:10-07:00","id":961897,"title":"","content":"I feel that Psychics are much more likely to be sorcerers rather then less likely. Its not so much a case of unlikely that you are two rare phenomena like the books suggest, but more that Sorcerers are inclined to search and take in those with Psychic powers as they always seem to display such a tradition in media, with shamans and mediums seeming to apprentice those who already have a talent with the supernatural. Its essentially what mages do, they find those who seem to naturally display powers and train them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T16:52:49-07:00","id":961980,"title":"","content":"I tend to make sorcerers a sort of middle ground in my games. Every supernatural power has a demi-race that are perfect as sorcerer covens. Kinians, kinfolk, ghouls/revenants, shih, thralls and mediums are all potentially powerful sorcerers with every reason to do so. I think sorcerers should have a much larger range of factions and conspiracies much like mage, where sorcerers from all over the world use different combinations of paths and psychic powers. I'd much rather the &quot;Hunter: the reckoning&quot; book be thrown out in favor of one dedicated to sorcerers and gifted mortals(who would do a much better job anyway).<br /> <br /> Idea's so sorcerer factions:<br /> <br /> Men in Black: The mortal government isn't even slightly ignorant of the supernatural world. The earth is a melting pot of unexplainable phenomena, nights are filled with the roars and wails of nightmares in open combat, monsters that manipulate entire cities, and alien horrors gaze on us from just outside our field of view. With a new &quot;world ending&quot; event every week the only thing keeping the public from devolving into a panicked frenzy is their own blissful ignorance, and the Men in Black like to keep it that way.<br /> <br /> Overseen and funded by a department of NATO and several private companies, the division of supernatural investigations focuses on covering up evidence of supernatural damage, investigating non-mundane crimes, and combating supernaturals on the physical, legal, and financial levels. They act in conjunction with powers like the camarilla, technocracy, and DNA, lend them their superior resources and manpower for knowledge of and weapons to fight against rogue supernaturals.<br /> <br /> The Seekers of Light: &quot;Knowledge is Power&quot;, this saying is truer in the world of darkness than many would first believe. Knowledge of science and the arcane has meant the difference between being a free man or slave of the darkness since ancient times and it hasn't changed yet. Under its clean, sophisticated skin the world is still ruled by the same demons as it was in medieval times and for all the same reasons. Monsters have power. They hide in the dark where mortals fear to tread, hording the wonders and mysteries of the universe for only themselves. Only the bravest and most foolish would step into the dark, yet that is what the seekers do every day. Seeking to snatch to secrets that lay within.<br /> <br /> As a long established order, the seekers work behind the scenes, searching for ancient knowledge and hidden treasures too tantalizing resist. They break into ancient crypts, hidden chantries, and even breach other worlds for the chance to at the score of their lives. Many would expect such a career to lower a persons life expectancy, and they'd be right, but the seekers have perfected the art. They sneak undetected from the mystic eyes of mages, they've survived fights with monsters, and when things go crazy, made getting the f*ck out of there into a science.<br /> <br /> The Faceless Web: The world is crazy. Our nightmares are real and they fill the night their with bloodcurdling howls. Strange lights appearing out of nowhere and disappearing before you can investigate. Roars and crunching bones leave behind bloody trails that are clean by next morning. Murder scenes left by men outrunning Lamborghini's are explained as gang violence. The monsters are everywhere, but they cover their tracks as soon as their made. But you know the truth, even if no one will believe you. You just need to find the right way to tell them.<br /> <br /> Humanity may not be a perfect race, but they aren't stupid. You can't have a world filled to the brim with supernatural weirdness occurring every day, and have no one notice. People are going to find out, and they going to try to tell everyone else. And when no one believes them, they'll look for other who know. The &quot;Deeper Web&quot; was made by these people. A series on anonymous Websites on the deep web made by a conglomerate of people from all races and backgrounds all trying to break the illusion that keeps the people from seeing the monsters. It's largest group, &quot;Faceless&quot;, operates behind a well known public website to gather information and uncover enough evidence of the supernatural to expose them to the public.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T18:13:24-07:00","id":962003,"title":"","content":"Very Cool Prometheas! It sounds like a good idea to mine Hunter the Vigil for ideas to import to the Classic World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> Back in the day I thought of Numina as a way to express supernatural martial arts, as a better system for Street Fighter in the World of Darkness. Basically a quicker more instinctive version of sorcery channeled through martial arts and meditation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T20:12:22-07:00","id":962044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/960537-which-gamelines-splats-do-you-want-to-incorporate-sorcerers-more-often?p=962003#post962003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Very Cool Prometheas! It sounds like a good idea to mine Hunter the Vigil for ideas to import to the Classic World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> Back in the day I thought of Numina as a way to express supernatural martial arts, as a better system for Street Fighter in the World of Darkness. Basically a quicker more instinctive version of sorcery channeled through martial arts and meditation.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think the chi arts of the shih in demon hunter x work to a more martial arts oriented character. Though they really aren't called such, the chi arts mentioned are similar to sorcerer/psychic numina in that they are paths anyone can learn, but instead of using willpower(psychic powers) or mana(sorcerer paths) they use the characters &quot;chi pool&quot;(basically their health, every two points of chi spent is a health level lost. something very dangerous for powers designed for mid to close combat)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T20:40:13-07:00","id":962047,"title":"","content":"Yeah I allow Mana background to be used as chi without using health.<br /> <br /> And I give the Shih access to Sorcery as well, with certain secret techniques and rituals used for unlocking psychic powers, think meditating while hovering above the ground for the classic super kung fu masters.<br /> <br /> Its interesting the Shih were founded by a Mage, so I have it at least one of the Shih per Generation is an awakened master, its just very rare because they only seldomly train someone who awakened, so it is often said the same handful of awakened keep reincarnating and finding their way back into the Shih.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T14:55:10-07:00","id":963926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/960537-which-gamelines-splats-do-you-want-to-incorporate-sorcerers-more-often?p=962047#post962047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah I allow Mana background to be used as chi without using health.<br /> <br /> And I give the Shih access to Sorcery as well, with certain secret techniques and rituals used for unlocking psychic powers, think meditating while hovering above the ground for the classic super kung fu masters.<br /> <br /> Its interesting the Shih were founded by a Mage, so I have it at least one of the Shih per Generation is an awakened master, its just very rare because they only seldomly train someone who awakened, so it is often said the same handful of awakened keep reincarnating and finding their way back into the Shih.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a good way to do it. Mana is basically Chi, so having that Background would enable them to channel Chi more efficiently.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T23:36:34-07:00","id":964111,"title":"","content":"Actually the only WoD game I don't think they fit in well is Mage--they are too similar. If I'm including them in another game I'm not going to include Mages and vice versa. If human magic users are going to play a big supporting role in a game, I'm more inclined to go with Mages; if the role is smaller, I'll go with Sorcerers because their systems are more straightforward and they don't draw so much narrative attention to themselves with fancy metaphysics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T07:11:42-07:00","id":964266,"title":"","content":"It is one of the high ironies of WoD that the best people to oppose Mages are Sorcerers because they have superior countermagic. In other gamelines, the countermagic becomes a more minor annoyance and sorcerers become more nuanced and subtle. Without the Mage cosmology, you can also turn Technological Numina into a form of Mad Science, which is always fun to introduce in any game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T19:21:43-07:00","id":970406,"title":"","content":"Any of them. Especially <i>Werewolf: The Apocalypse</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T20:00:54-07:00","id":970432,"title":"","content":"To be more specific: WtA needs more 'self-contained' nemeses, and hedge mages fit the bill of 'evil sorcerer bargaining with the Wyrm for power'. Really, WtA needs a way to better simulate Pentex higher-ups than &quot;Here's a smorgasbord of crossover stuff&quot;. <br /> <br /> How exactly, are fomori created? I mean in-setting, that is. Pentex is not Black Spiral-only, so---how do they summon the Banes they need? Gifts are for Fera and Kinfolk, so: how?<br /> <br /> Hedge mages solve these problems quite nicely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T20:52:28-07:00","id":970454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/960537-which-gamelines-splats-do-you-want-to-incorporate-sorcerers-more-often?p=970432#post970432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be more specific: WtA needs more 'self-contained' nemeses, and hedge mages fit the bill of 'evil sorcerer bargaining with the Wyrm for power'. Really, WtA needs a way to better simulate Pentex higher-ups than &quot;Here's a smorgasbord of crossover stuff&quot;.<br /> <br /> How exactly, are fomori created? I mean in-setting, that is. Pentex is not Black Spiral-only, so---how do they summon the Banes they need? Gifts are for Fera and Kinfolk, so: how?<br /> <br /> Hedge mages solve these problems quite nicely.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pentex doesn't need to summon banes. Human society tends to attract them pretty readily without their interference, and one bad day can catapult them into someone. Project Iliad need only get someone to act out in a certain manner to attract a bane, or produce noxious poisons that attract elemental banes; if there are any banes (no guarantees that the chemicals won't just melt you to death instead), they'll take care of the rest. The higher-ups that have some deal with the devil can just have arbitrary benefits; it doesn't matter how, say, someone's unaging status is defined, just that they are unaging.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T21:59:29-07:00","id":970485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/960537-which-gamelines-splats-do-you-want-to-incorporate-sorcerers-more-often?p=970454#post970454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Pentex doesn't need to summon banes. Human society tends to attract them pretty readily without their interference, and one bad day can catapult them into someone. Project Iliad need only get someone to act out in a certain manner to attract a bane, or produce noxious poisons that attract elemental banes; if there are any banes (no guarantees that the chemicals won't just melt you to death instead), they'll take care of the rest. The higher-ups that have some deal with the devil can just have arbitrary benefits; it doesn't matter how, say, someone's unaging status is defined, just that they are unaging.</div> </div> </div> </div>That seems haphazard and not as satisfying. I like the whole, they keep mad scientists and sorcerers on staff, as well as random powers like immortality because of Deal with the Wyrmdevil.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T22:11:38-07:00","id":970487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/960537-which-gamelines-splats-do-you-want-to-incorporate-sorcerers-more-often?p=970485#post970485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That seems haphazard and not as satisfying. I like the whole, they keep mad scientists and sorcerers on staff, as well as random powers like immortality because of Deal with the Wyrmdevil.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's the state of the world, such as it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T05:23:00-07:00","id":970632,"title":"","content":"Fomori creation is covered in detail in Possessed and, to a lesser extent, Freak Legion. While Freak Legion was a dedicated fomori book, it was light on the creation rules. Yes, I completely support using sorcerers (and psychics) in WtA because they offer unique challenges, especially if they have entered Souk Pacts with something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T09:47:25-07:00","id":970751,"title":"","content":"Oh, I know about fomori creation, but I'm referring to <i>in-setting</i>. If it was as as simple as 'human nature attracts Banes and they do the rest', then we'd have about a billion fomori on Earth right now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T11:51:53-07:00","id":970810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Faradn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/960537-which-gamelines-splats-do-you-want-to-incorporate-sorcerers-more-often?p=964111#post964111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually the only WoD game I don't think they fit in well is Mage--they are too similar. If I'm including them in another game I'm not going to include Mages and vice versa. If human magic users are going to play a big supporting role in a game, I'm more inclined to go with Mages; if the role is smaller, I'll go with Sorcerers because their systems are more straightforward and they don't draw so much narrative attention to themselves with fancy metaphysics.</div> </div> </div> </div>As much as I have a twisted relationship with Mage that's mostly-love intertwined with a thick network of hate-y vines, I have to agree with Faradn 100%. I'd just ditch Mage-style mages and have all &quot;mages&quot; be sorcerers be the &quot;humans who are playing the hard game&quot; trying to stand toe-to-toe with the other supernaturals. <br /> <br /> There are fundamental mechanical reasons to do so: Mage's Paradox as a ridiculously overwrought system that every other game covers in a much neater, tighter and more open to the specifics of the situation (e.g. &quot;You botched! Okay, here's what happened&quot;), Mage's power stat being, effectively half-powered (it's pretty much 2-5, as 6+ Arete games are in the same category as high end Elder games in Vampire and the like) meaning that success-for-success comparisons are either really disadvantageous for mages or just completely off-kilter, and so on. Fundamentally something like Sorcerer would just WORK better than trying to shoehorn Mage magic into a set of systems that interlock or work vis-a-vis each other more effectively. <br /> <br /> Conversely, a lot of the metaphysics of Mage, which hit significant road bumps when confronting the &quot;absolutes&quot; of the other systems, would be freed up in a Mage game without sorcerers and without VtM vampires, WtF werewovles, etc. It's hard to trumpet &quot;Belief structures Reality&quot; when, well, it just, DOESN'T unless you carefully avoid everything for which what is, is..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T13:14:08-07:00","id":970868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/960537-which-gamelines-splats-do-you-want-to-incorporate-sorcerers-more-often?p=970751#post970751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, I know about fomori creation, but I'm referring to <i>in-setting</i>. If it was as as simple as 'human nature attracts Banes and they do the rest', then we'd have about a billion fomori on Earth right now.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was one of the reasons why I first started to introduce Humanity to non-Vampire games. I generally ruled that Banes were not interested in anyone with a Humanity greater than the Willpower of the Bane and, when resisting possession, characters got to use the higher of their Humanity or Willpower to resist. Of course, not everyone would be interested in integrating Humanity (and, by extension, Virtues) into their games, so possession becomes more random.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T15:12:59-07:00","id":970938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/960537-which-gamelines-splats-do-you-want-to-incorporate-sorcerers-more-often?p=970751#post970751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, I know about fomori creation, but I'm referring to <i>in-setting</i>. If it was as as simple as 'human nature attracts Banes and they do the rest', then we'd have about a billion fomori on Earth right now.</div> </div> </div> </div>There has to be that &quot;worst day ever&quot; trigger to force the two together. Unfortunately, the modern world can make it way more common than it might have been before.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T17:27:59-07:00","id":971008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/960537-which-gamelines-splats-do-you-want-to-incorporate-sorcerers-more-often?p=970938#post970938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There has to be that &quot;worst day ever&quot; trigger to force the two together. Unfortunately, the modern world can make it way more common than it might have been before.</div> </div> </div> </div>Um. Considering times like the dark ages, (when leprosy and plagues were a norm, lower classes were slaves to higher nobles, and the kings/high nobles could do whatever they wanted to you be it forcibly bedding your wife to killing your kids for no consequence) I'm rather certain that the modern age is better than all that came before. Especially in WOD when supernaturals back then had a free pass to waltz into your house in broad daylight and eat your family. While boring, modern life isn't THAT bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T17:48:22-07:00","id":971028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/960537-which-gamelines-splats-do-you-want-to-incorporate-sorcerers-more-often?p=971008#post971008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Um. Considering times like the dark ages, (when leprosy and plagues were a norm, lower classes were slaves to higher nobles, and the kings/high nobles could do whatever they wanted to you be it forcibly bedding your wife to killing your kids for no consequence) I'm rather certain that the modern age is better than all that came before. Especially in WOD when supernaturals back then had a free pass to waltz into your house in broad daylight and eat your family. While boring, modern life isn't THAT bad.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are we going for Dung Ages over actual day to day life in the era? While lacking in medicine and numerous other areas, it also had a lot fewer people for banes to torment. Whereas, with over 7 billion people, many working jobs that are no less shit than in the bad old days with regard to what it does for them psychologically, you get trainloads full of fomori just by accident.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}